note=p/"SHORT_K_BOTH_TYPE_I_LOCALIZATION-v1.md";assert not note.exists();note.write_text("# Short dual window and the remaining two TypeI columns\n\nPost-publication research only, 6 November 2026. This note is outside the frozen 333-page release (Main b6e1571219d92432454ffd1afac2c812a9f28b9e / Pages 6b3565d4e76c46a07cad6b32ef4b21274e800493). It is a corollary and quantitative localization of already proved partial estimates, not a bound for the remaining kernel. The new estimate in this run is the actual finite large-k bound in lane-b/FINITE_K_CUBIC_BANDS-v1.md, not the bookkeeping below. No new sieve theorem, scalar input, zero assertion, Lean or GRH result is supplied.\n\nAcceptance criteria: reconstruct the original finite kernel without losing any coefficient state or mean; justify each discarded sector by its independently reviewed bound; derive the simultaneous scale/frequency/deletion windows; distinguish the original pair from auxiliary deletion terms. Check the rational exponents independently and obtain adversarial review. A conditional input or exact localization must never be described as the missing signed estimate.\n\n## 1. Sources and actual object\n\nUse the accepted direct-discrete top-prefix reduction, the Gauss large-short-divisor theorem and the HB-v2 balanced-TypeII theorem from the preceding Gauss-book milestone, together with this run's finite-k cubic-band theorem and the exact TypeI deletion transfer. Their exact files and SHA256 values are frozen by the companion source-pins JSON. The physical cubic large sieve remains the pinned external input of those theorems; nothing here reproves it or imports another moment theorem.\n\nWork in the ORIGINAL unweighted pure two-pivot block, A2=1 and the other good factors units, A1 comparable to H=D^(3/4), X=D^(3/8), V=X^(1/6)/2, D>=2^64. Keep the original allowed high window for U, one FIXED possibly complex W supported[1,2] and zero at endpoints, B=||W||infinity and M(W)=(2pi)^(-1) integral|What(it)|dt. All constants and epsilon losses have the same fixed nu,S,source/ray and profile qualifications as the parent theorems.\n\nP_X[AU,AU] denotes the actual top-prefix object normalized ONCE by 1/D. Its direct reduction is to L_X^K[AY,AY], with Y=min(U,D^(1/8)), original finite K=sqrt(b_cap), all e|P_S, all Nw<64, every all-rho/source/root component and the EXACT set\nT_X={(w,s): s good, V<Ns<=2V, Nw(Ns)^6<=X}.\nThere is no counting-density mean replacement or principal-mode projection. s is arbitrary, and neither (k,s)=1 nor (w,s)=1 is imposed. Fixed S conductor drops never restore a raw zero. Optional original unequal-norm projection retains each full equal-norm ideal fibre.\n\nPut J0=D^(1/32). If K<=J0, the large-k sector is empty. Otherwise use the accepted finite literal dyadic bound for J0<Nk<=K. In either case the surviving original cutoff is Nk<=min(K,J0). This is not Euler completion.\n\n## 2. The rigorous sector reduction\n\nThe direct reduction and large-short-divisor bound give errors with critical powers -1/16,3/4,31/48, up to the stated epsilon and B/profile factors. If Y=U, the coefficient-tail difference is EXACTLY zero.\n\nThe finite large-k theorem bounds the normalized discarded leading sector by\nB^2 (D K X)^epsilon A1 V [J0^(-2)+(D J0)^(-1)+D^(-1/3)J0^(-4/3)+Lambda/J0],\nLambda=A1 X/D^2.\nIts four powers are 3/4,-7/32,7/16,-3/32. Thus this sector is target-sized without a separate-column absolute-k triangle. It does not cancel the short-k mean.\n\nExpand the FULL AY coefficient exactly by the accepted short-factor/HB identity. In particular retain its constant/subtraction states; do not replace AY by just a double short-divisor sum. Keep the exact ideal squarefreeness/coprimality, actual dyadic boxes and HB signs. The accepted HB-v2 estimate makes every term with at least one balanced TypeII column target-sized (normalized leading power at most11/16 at Y=D^(1/8)). Restricting its original finite k set further does not increase the positive majorant used in that theorem. Its coefficient1 long-factor classification requires D>=2^64, which has been imposed.\n\nDefine R_short,I,I to be the finite sum of ALL remaining accepted expansion terms: both columns are TypeI, all original AY coefficient states and HB signs remain, and Nk<=min(K,J0). This is a signed complex component, not a positive energy or an asserted lower bound. The parent results yield\n|P_X[AU,AU]-R_short,I,I|\n <<_(fixed data,epsilon) (B^2+B M(W)) D^epsilon H.\nFinite dyadic/HB/source-component logarithms are included in epsilon. The same assertion for the historical counting mean, the whole h1 form or every other block does NOT follow. This is a sufficient reduction of this actual top piece only. No necessity for any separately split component or the final signed assembly is asserted.\n\n## 3. Simultaneous windows in one surviving TypeI column\n\nWrite its original ideal m=a*b*u*v with Na,Nb<=Y, P=NaNb, c=u*v, and u the grouped short HB factors. The long v has coefficient1; u retains the actual signed divisor-bounded HB coefficients. On each active TypeI box,\nP<=D^(1/4), Nu<=C (D/P)^(1/3), T=D/(P Nu),\nwhere C is fixed by the at-most-nine-factor decomposition. Nv is comparable to T with the original sharp interval conventions.\n\nOn a NONZERO original branch, a,b,u,k are good squarefree and pairwise coprime. Otherwise an original squarefree or eta(k^2) raw zero has already killed it. The exact growing cubic frequency in the accepted finite fixed-twist package is t=a*b*u*k. It is not the other full column or an arbitrary character label. Therefore\nT>=c D^(1/2),\nNt=P Nu Nk<=C D^(1/3) P^(2/3) D^(1/32)<=C D^(17/32),\nT Nt=D Nk<=D^(33/32).\nThe product identity is EXACT for the chosen profile scale T, not just a comparison of exponents. Bounded dyadic/capacity constants are retained in interval sizes, not used to alter these exponent statements.\n\nFor the other original column n, the full good deletion ideal in that TypeI factor is\nQ=rad(a*b*u*n*k*s*w)\nwith all additional fixed exclusions retained exactly as in the parent psi/goodness functions. Since Nn<=2D, Ns<=2V<=D^(1/16), Nw<64,\nNQ<=C (P Nu)(Nn)(Nk)(Ns)(Nw)<=C D^(51/32).\nThis is a deletion-ideal bound, NOT a new primitive conductor bound. The original pair modulus m*n has size comparable to D^2. Original common-prime and S/ray zeros stay deleted regardless of primitive conductor drops.\n\nOpening (v,Q)=1 by the exact transfer, only d|rad Q with (d,t)=1 and Nd<2T can be active. The shifted frequency d*t is again squarefree, and\n(T/Nd) N(d*t)=T Nt=D Nk,\nN(d*t)<2 T Nt<=2 D^(33/32).\nThe full Q sum and its signs are retained. For T/Nd in(1/2,1), count the literal unit directly; below or at1/2 the endpoint-zero profile gives zero. Thus a proposed sharp-interval Gauss input after opening deletions must cover this coupled hyperbolic scale/frequency range and the bounded subunit case. A theorem only uniform up to the pre-deletion D^(17/32) frequency range would not suffice after this transfer.\n\n## 4. Shared-frequency geometry and the unresolved estimate\n\nBefore an auxiliary deletion or common-divisor opening, take TWO surviving original coprime columns\nm=a1*b1*u1*v1, n=a2*b2*u2*v2.\nTheir prefix ideals a1*b1*u1 and a2*b2*u2 are coprime; k is coprime to both full columns on a nonzero branch. The two frequencies t1=(a1*b1*u1)k and t2=(a2*b2*u2)k consequently have ideal gcd EXACTLY k. This does not make their phases independent or centered. The same short k and exact w/s/root/ray means still couple the two long sums.\n\nThis gcd statement is restricted to the original branch. Auxiliary d terms can have overlapping column prefixes; after shifting t to d*t it cannot be reused without their actual overlap factors. Full-union deletions cannot be replaced by a reduced quotient conductor. Equal rational norms are not single ideals or orthogonal columns.\n\nThe two TypeI columns, their fixed-twist Gauss factors, the shared short k and ALL finite w/e/s/rho/source/root components remain unestimated jointly before positive divisor or conductor triangles. The conditional H(alpha,beta) diagnostic in lane A is still an unavailable sufficient input, not a theorem or a necessary condition. A uniform box description and an exact shared gcd do not prove a power saving.\n\nThe next genuine estimate must address this actual coupled short-k BOTH-TypeI kernel (or its signed discrete discrepancy), with original coefficients, sharp intervals, common profile and full masks. Whole signed13/12, global unsigned9/8, the separate short/principal assembly, independent determinant/zero-location bridges and the distinct Dirichlet/Hecke/Dedekind/elliptic/general Artin/Lean obligations remain OPEN.\n")
